Vendored blueprint-compiler
===========================

The `blueprintcompiler/` directory is an unmodified copy of the
blueprint-compiler Python package, version v0.22.2:

  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/blueprint-compiler
  tag v0.22.2

blueprint-compiler is Copyright 2021-2025 James Westman and contributors,
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later
(SPDX: LGPL-3.0-or-later). The full license text is in COPYING beside this
file, and every vendored source file keeps its original license header.

Protota does not link against or derive from this code. It is executed
unmodified as a standalone tool inside a Pyodide (CPython/WebAssembly)
interpreter in a Web Worker, the same way CI executes the distro-packaged
`blueprint-compiler` binary. The version is pinned to match the Fedora 45
container used by the `blueprint-export` CI job (blueprint-compiler
0.22.2-1.fc45), so browser-side syntax results track the host compiler CI
treats as the authority.

Files added by Protota (not part of upstream, licensed like the rest of
this repository):

  gi/__init__.py      - minimal import-time stub for PyGObject's `gi`
                        module. blueprintcompiler/gir.py imports gi at
                        module import time; the stub satisfies those
                        imports so the tokenizer and parser can run.
                        There is no GObject introspection in the browser:
                        any attempt to actually use GIRepository raises.
                        Consequently only *syntax*-level checking runs in
                        the browser; GIR-backed validation (types,
                        properties, signals) remains host-only.
  blueprint_check.py  - driver that tokenizes and parses a .blp source and
                        returns parse errors as JSON, deliberately skipping
                        the AST validation pass that requires typelibs.
  manifest.json       - list of files the worker loads into the Pyodide
                        filesystem.
  NOTICE              - this file.

Upgrading: re-vendor `blueprintcompiler/` from the tag matching the version
installed by .github/workflows/deploy.yml's `blueprint-export` job, then
regenerate manifest.json (see the note inside it).
